  "body": "## Result\n\nComplete negative answer to the exact universal biconstrained symmetry question: `abs(psi(13/27,14/27) - psi(14/27,13/27)) >= 1/108`. Disposition: **claimed_solved, 3/5 substantive author turns**, using the complete-earlier exception.\n\nThe exact rational-boundary formula in `TURN_3.md` covers every finite admissible graph and supplies matching rational blow-ups. The credited seven-type matrix from Chudnovsky\u2013Hompe\u2013Scott\u2013Seymour\u2013Spirkl, EJC 29(2) (2022), P2.47, Figure 1, bounds the two integer incidence minima by four; incompatible denominators prove asymmetry. Actual psi values and their ordering are unevaluated. The two 162-vertex examples provide upper bounds only.\n\n## Evidence and credit\n\n- Exact original source: Seymour, OWR 1/2019, pp46\u201347, with all four degree constraints and distinct reachable vertices\n- Full independent AI-assisted source/proof review: PASS without mandatory correction; 43,755 author assertions replayed and 2,552 independently written controls\n- All 30 frozen author files and eight review files preserved byte-for-byte, with additive publication status and manifest\n- Source matrix and classical framework credited; no historical novelty certification or human peer-review claim\n\nStart at [PUBLICATION_STATUS.md](unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004048/PUBLICATION_STATUS.md), then the full third-turn proof and independent review. OpenAI tools assisted research, proof drafting, verification and review.\n\n## Scope of changes\n\nFresh-main integration retaining the frozen author checkpoint as second parent. Only this target's 41 artifacts and its own QUEUE row change. Raw source PDFs and imported records are excluded. Draft only; no merge or release requested.",
